== a project include pinned
no findings

== a project include by tag
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include project group/ci is not pinned to a commit SHA: ref is v1.2.3
fix: set ref: to a full 40-character commit SHA, with the version in a comment (ref: <sha> # v1.2.3)

== a project include without ref
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include project group/ci is not pinned to a commit SHA: ref is (no ref: the default branch)
fix: set ref: to a full 40-character commit SHA, with the version in a comment (ref: <sha> # v1.2.3)

== a component pinned
no findings

== a component by version
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include component $CI_SERVER_FQDN/group/lint/golangci@1.2.0 is not pinned to a commit SHA
fix: pin the component to a full 40-character commit SHA, with the version in a comment (component: <path>@<sha> # 1.2.0)

== a component at ~latest
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include component gitlab.com/group/lint/golangci@~latest is not pinned to a commit SHA
fix: pin the component to a full 40-character commit SHA, with the version in a comment (component: <path>@<sha> # 1.2.0)

== a remote include with integrity
no findings

== a remote include without integrity
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include remote https://example.com/ci.yml has no integrity:
fix: add integrity: sha256-<base64 of the file's SHA-256 digest>, or copy the file into the repository and include it with local:

== a remote include as a string
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include remote https://example.com/ci.yml has no integrity:
fix: add integrity: sha256-<base64 of the file's SHA-256 digest>, or copy the file into the repository and include it with local:

== a template include cannot be pinned
file: .gitlab-ci.yml
message: line 2: include template Jobs/SAST.gitlab-ci.yml cannot be pinned: GitLab serves the version of the instance
fix: copy the template into the repository and include it with local:, or include the matching CI/CD component pinned to a commit SHA

